### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
**KEY CONSIDERATIONS:**
1. Conservative approach applied: When uncertain about whether a study met criteria, particularly regarding follow-up 
duration or renal assessment specificity, studies were included for further review.

2. Several studies had borderline sample sizes (20-25 participants) but were included when they clearly assessed 
long-term renal outcomes.

3. Some reviews (Study 36, 59) were included because they provided valuable data synthesis on nephrotoxic treatments 
even though they were secondary analyses.

4. Studies focusing on acute toxicity during treatment were excluded per protocol requiring ≥1 year post-treatment 
cessation assessment.

5. The included studies cover all major nephrotoxic modalities: nephrectomy (Wilms tumor primarily), cisplatin 
(neuroblastoma, germ cell tumors, osteosarcoma), ifosfamide (sarcomas), and radiation/TBI (hematologic malignancies).

6. Confidence ratings reflect certainty that each study meets all inclusion criteria. "Medium" confidence assigned to 
studies where some uncertainty exists about exact follow-up timing or completeness of renal assessment.

