Studies excluded for reasons including: wrong population (adults), wrong outcome (not renal function), insufficient 
follow-up (<1 year), sample size <20, review articles, case reports, methodology articles, or unclear eligibility.

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):

SCREENING METHODOLOGY:
- Conservative approach applied: when in doubt, studies were INCLUDED
- Each study was evaluated against all selection criteria
- Studies were excluded for the following reasons:
  * Wrong population (adults, not childhood cancer): Studies 7, 22, 25, 30, 42, 47, 49, 57, 67, 68, 74, 78, 79, 87, 93, 
97, 99
  * Wrong outcome (not renal function): Studies 5, 6, 19, 20, 23, 34, 41, 56, 61, 63, 65, 69, 92, 94, 95
  * Insufficient follow-up (<1 year after treatment): Studies 3, 10, 14, 16, 18, 24, 32, 33, 52, 64, 83
  * Sample size <20: Studies 17, 38, 91
  * Review/methodology articles: Studies 8, 13, 21, 28, 37, 46, 50, 53, 54, 58, 60, 77, 84, 88, 89, 90, 100
  * Letter to editor: Study 96
  * Unclear eligibility: Studies 27, 36, 40, 45, 55, 59, 80, 81, 82, 86, 98

KEY DECISIONS:
- TBI was considered as involving kidney region when specifically assessed for renal toxicity (Studies 9, 43, 62)
- Studies reporting renal function as part of broader late effects were included if they met other criteria (Studies 12,
26, 35, 51)
- Adult survivors of childhood cancer were included when they reported on renal function after childhood treatment 
(Study 73)

