  microsomes. Orphenadrine (a CYP2B6 inhibitor) and anti-CYP2B IgG inhibited microsomal cyclophosphamide hydroxylation  
  to a greater extent than ifosphamide hydroxylation, consistent with the 8-fold higher activity of complementary       
  DNA-expressed CYP2B6 with cyclophosphamide. In contrast, troleandomycin, a selective inhibitor of CYP3A3 and -3A4,    
