│ risk of complications, we treated relapsed or refractory leukemia patients with TBI administered in fractionated,    │
│ parallel opposed large fields with 24 MV photons, using tissue compensation and partial-transmission lung shielding. │
│ Tissue toxicities were then determined. RESULTS Dose quantitation in bone-equivalent and tissue-equivalent phantoms  │
│ demonstrated that backscatter and pair production interactions adjacent to bone increased the bone marrow dose by 6  │
│ to 11%. At an SSD of 400 cm and at patient diameters of 20 to 40 cm, the percent inhomogeneity across the phantom    │
│ with 24 MV photons was 0 to 0.3%, compared to 4 to 6% for 6 MV photons. End-organ toxicities consisted of clinical   │
