│ significantly increased after treatment with both anthracyclines and cardiac irradiation (12.6%; 95% CI, 4.3% to     │
│ 20.3%), after anthracyclines (7.3%; 95% CI, 3.8% to 10.7%), and after cardiac irradiation (4.0%; 95% CI, 0.5% to     │
│ 7.4%) compared with other treatments. In the proportional hazards analyses, anthracycline (dose), cardiac            │
│ irradiation (dose), combination of these treatments, and congenital heart disease were significantly associated with │
