│ 0.5 SD (range −1.5 to + 2.2, n= 22), and at follow‐up −0.3 SD (range −3.9 to + 2.6, n= 61). The mean calculated      │
│ decrease in relative kidney size was 0.1 SD unit per year during the follow‐up time. The median glomerular           │
│ filtration rate was 110 ml/min/1.73 m2 (range 70 to 164). Six of 60 patients had glomerular filtration rates below   │
│ 85 ml/min/1.73 m2. Three patients had some evidence of tubular dysfunction documented by increased excretion of      │
│ urinary amino acids and/or beta‐2‐micro‐globulin or by reduced concentrating capacity. In spite of these             │
